"smart_blocks:Computer Science/C++/C++ Friendship (friend keyword).md#FF5582A6;\"> Friendship is not reciprocal. If class `A` declares class `B` as a friend, `B` can access `A`'s private/protected members, but `A` cannot automatically access `B`'s private/protected members. To achieve mutual friendship, both classes must explicitly declare each other as friends.</mark>#{1}": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.05847677,-0.02923777,-0.06846594,-0.04109043,-0.09048259,-0.02796309,0.03625339,0.01721678,0.0538106,-0.05051376,0.02510468,-0.00876957,0.06633138,0.0085866,0.01941642,0.02648546,-0.05004891,0.07669359,-0.0653129,0.02136412,0.08903068,-0.07488207,-0.01049827,-0.0494255,0.03781728,0.11568225,-0.02202983,-0.06494026,-0.00218518,-0.18421653,-0.02445945,-0.04022227,0.01094942,0.00508739,-0.009441,0.03183651,0.02084149,-0.01374317,-0.00993577,0.05894051,-0.0100956,0.0239682,0.03068785,-0.06016137,-0.00356905,0.01954352,0.00519106,0.02692822,0.01820921,-0.02680521,-0.00772392,0.02144331,-0.02460658,0.06769193,-0.03045132,0.11883753,0.06844598,0.0357837,0.01123215,0.04355705,0.03746161,0.0620008,-0.11219077,0.0648483,-0.02292693,0.0578293,-0.00220216,-0.02452065,0.02750679,0.03674883,0.01983764,0.07973468,0.02032346,0.03977949,0.04435663,-0.03000514,-0.01432851,0.00713326,-0.02191841,-0.01359137,-0.05170415,-0.06376431,0.03477727,0.02095629,-0.01417148,0.03264039,0.01018066,-0.12694122,0.01345443,0.02753389,-0.07303778,-0.04202692,0.03382509,0.03289089,-0.01383916,0.00740354,-0.01390654,-0.01637243,-0.100265,0.13281648,-0.09105915,0.04669311,0.02885719,-0.01427667,0.03228609,-0.02571628,0.01151104,-0.00913734,0.00883789,-0.05571358,-0.02938109,-0.04306475,0.00013466,-0.06632173,-0.041321,0.00516053,0.06061767,-0.02971892,-0.02322842,-0.04335385,0.04251579,0.03161475,0.03182863,0.01431586,-0.01056961,-0.06676531,0.04215952,0.0630837,0.02381436,0.02360589,-0.00930362,-0.01695775,0.01485465,-0.09016273,-0.03180453,0.03754775,-0.03792404,-0.0542